# LinHT has no permanent network uplink. The only IP link is the usb0 gadget,
# and there LinHT is the DHCP server, not a client - systemd-timesyncd would
# never reach a time server and would just keep retrying. The clock is left to
# the RTC and to userspace (GPS), so keep the NTP client switched off.
#
# systemd itself ships 90-systemd.preset containing
#     enable systemd-timesyncd.service
# Preset files are read in lexicographic order and the first matching line
# wins, so this file has to sort before 90-systemd.preset.
disable systemd-timesyncd.service
